# The release this source came from, for a build that has no git history to
# ask -- a release tarball, a "Download ZIP", any unpacked source archive.
#
# .gitattributes marks this file export-subst, so git archive rewrites the
# last line below into what `git describe --tags` says about the commit the
# archive was made from: a release tag on its own, or a release tag with the
# number of commits past it and the commit. The build reduces that to the
# version it reports, "2026-11-R1" or "2026-11-R1+22" -- the same two forms a
# git checkout reports. host/cmake/set_release.cmake does it for the host
# tools and firmware/version.mk for the firmware images.
#
# In a git checkout nothing has rewritten it, so the last line is still the
# placeholder git wrote it as. A checkout's version comes from git directly
# and this file is not read at all.
#
# Nothing here has to be edited before a release: the tag the release is made
# from is what git fills in.
$Format:%(describe:tags,match=[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]-R[0-9]*,match=[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]-RC[0-9]*,match=[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]-[0-9][0-9]-DEV[0-9]*)$
